Part A: W_{AI^Kt}(empty) can exceed 1 (Prop 2.3(ii) assumes <= 1); the correct general bound is t(m0).
 |W|   m0  a*  family weight    t(m0)
   4    4   3         0.3454       64
   4   10   3         3.4485     1000
   8   10   3         0.1745     1000
   4   10   5       344.8535   100000
  -> a family of 2^-|W|-weighted deciders reaches total weight > 1; Kraft gives only W(0) <= t(m0).

Part B: c_p measured against t(|chi| + |p|): partial sums of the family's weights (uncapped vs capped at c_p >= 1).
 a*    N_max   sum (uncapped)   sum (capped)
  2       10            0.659       0.056641
  2      100            0.884       0.061813
  2     1000            1.058       0.062436
  2    10000            1.211       0.062493
  2   100000            1.364       0.062499
  3       10            8.460       0.056641
  3      100           20.382       0.061813
  3     1000           93.316       0.062436
  3    10000          697.647       0.062493
  3   100000         6562.916       0.062499
  -> uncapped sums grow without bound (a* = 3: about 2^-|W| per group, i.e. ~ 2^-|W| N_max; a* = 2: ~ log N_max): the prior is
     not normalisable, so 'measuring against t(|chi|+|p|)' needs weight 2^-|p|/max(1, c_p).

Part C: log2 c_p of a padded Craig decider vs the floor log2(|q|/t(m0)) every program pays.
  cost model: alpha = 2.0, simulation exponent a = 2, t(m) = m^3, m0 = 4
       |q|    floor  notes bound  early exit  notes-floor  early-floor
        16    -2.00         3.78       -1.19         5.78         0.81
       128     1.00         9.11        1.13         8.11         0.13
      1024     4.00        15.01        4.02        11.01         0.02
      8192     7.00        21.00        7.00        14.00         0.00
     65536    10.00        27.00       10.00        17.00         0.00
    524288    13.00        33.00       13.00        20.00         0.00
   4194304    16.00        39.00       16.00        23.00         0.00
  33554432    19.00        45.00       19.00        26.00         0.00
 268435456    22.00        51.00       22.00        29.00         0.00
  -> the notes' bound charges (a - 1) log2|q| bits above the floor (growing); the early-exit decider stays a
     bounded number of bits above it, so P1b costs log2|f| + O(1), exactly the charge every program pays.
